course: dictionary
lesson: 10239
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must use context to choose the right one. Toilet is one of these words. «The bathroom has its own good habits: your own toothbrush, the toilet lid down...» Here toilet means the large bowl with a seat that you use, not the whole room.
explain: Sometimes toilet means the room instead. «To go to the toilet in a lesson, you ask politely and come back quickly.» You do not sit in a bowl in the classroom. You go to the room that has a toilet in it. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then test it in the sentence.
explain: Other places use other words for the same thing. In the US, «May I use the restroom?» means the same as asking to go to the toilet. In Australia, dunny is an informal word for toilet. In French, «Je peux aller aux toilettes, s'il vous plaît ?» means "May I go to the toilet, please?"
fact: A toilet is a large bowl with a seat that you use to get rid of wee and poo, then flush with water.
fact: Toilet can also mean the room that has a toilet in it, as in «To go to the toilet in a lesson, you ask politely».
fact: After using the toilet, flush it, then wash your hands with soap for about 20 seconds to remove germs.
fact: Never flush toys or wipes down the toilet, and little children should not play near toilets.
fact: «Comfort station» is an official American word for a public toilet, for example in a park.
exercise: In «To go to the toilet in a lesson, you ask politely», what does toilet mean? | Old washing and dressing | *A room with a toilet in it | A bath with hot water | A large bowl with a seat
exercise: What should you do after using the toilet? | Leave the lid up and go | Flush a wet wipe to be tidy | *Flush, then wash your hands with soap for about 20 seconds
exercise: In the US, what might you say to ask for the toilet? | *May I use the restroom? | Where is the bus stop? | I am going to the park | Please may I borrow a pencil?
test: Which word means a public toilet in America, for example in a park? | Dunny | *Comfort station | Loo bowl | Lid
test: Which is a safe thing to do? | Play near the toilets at break | Flush a toy down the toilet | *Wash your hands with soap for about 20 seconds after using the toilet
exam: In «The bathroom has its own good habits: your own toothbrush, the toilet lid down...», what does toilet mean? | A toothbrush holder | A bath with hot water | A bedroom with a bed | *The large bowl with a seat that you use to get rid of wee and poo
